{
  "_comment": [
    "The palm beach (notes/palm-beach-design.md): an island's coast from about eight under the waterline to",
    "about twelve over, in a warm or hot Age. Where in the climate it goes is biome_home/palm_beach.json; this",
    "is what it is once there. One biome for the beach and the lagoon, so the reef is its own and the white",
    "floor runs under clear water rather than meeting a warm ocean's yellow one in a seam.",
    "",
    "Vanilla beach's lists for every step but two. Its sand, clay and gravel disks are gone from the ores step,",
    "since a yellow disk under a white lagoon is the seam this biome exists to avoid. And the vegetation step",
    "is the warm ocean's reef -- coral, warm seagrass, sea pickles -- with sugar cane, and the palms. Turtles",
    "on the sand, parrots in the palms, and dolphins, nautilus and tropical fish in the lagoon, at a little more",
    "than vanilla's share of dolphins.",
    "",
    "Colours retuned on two walks (Jonah, 2026-10-01): the water tried aquamarine and came back to its first",
    "pale aqua ('too green'); the sky went from a pale cyan to a deep azure and then deeper still, far under",
    "vanilla's light #78a7ff, with the clouds whiter and more solid over it (`PalmDusk`)."
  ],
